WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.179
Matthew Fox was on a major career roll for
two decades.

00:00:03.179 --> 00:00:08.330
He headlined not one but two popular shows
in a row, with six seasons of the family drama

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:13.670
Party of Five and then six more years on the
sci-fi mystery phenomenon Lost not long after.

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:17.990
As a result of this pair of beloved series,
he had the rare distinction of being both

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:22.900
a heartthrob and a guy's guy, and seemed poised
to launch from his wild island adventures

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:24.460
straight into the big time.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:29.119
But the 2010s haven't been so kind to Fox,
despite some notable big screen efforts on

00:00:29.119 --> 00:00:30.119
his part.

00:00:30.119 --> 00:00:36.340
Here are a few theories that explore why,
lately, Matthew Fox has seemed so …

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:37.820
He broke big on TV

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:42.480
Fox established himself as a television star
thanks to his turns as Charlie Salinger and

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:43.480
Jack Shepherd.

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:47.460
The small screen was his home from the get-go,
having just a few film credits to his name

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:50.480
by the time Lost catapulted him into the spotlight.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:54.790
But the silver screen still piqued his interest,
and he tried out supporting roles in movies

00:00:54.790 --> 00:00:57.220
like Smokin' Aces and We Are Marshall.

00:00:57.220 --> 00:01:00.940
Neither of those were massive hits, but they
did suggest that there might be a place for

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:02.210
him in the movie biz.

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:07.120
Unfortunately, a controversial show ending
can follow an actor around like a dark cloud.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:12.370
And few people would argue that Lost's finale
was perhaps the worst show ending of all time.

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:17.110
It wasn't Fox's fault that the series ended
on such a confusing and frustrating note.

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:21.010
But as the face of the series, there's a chance
the blame could've fallen on him a little,

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:23.330
too — at least where ticket-buyers were
concerned.

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:27.500
With audiences as upset as they were about
the series' crazy conclusion, there's a very

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:31.110
real chance that some Fox fatigue set in as
part of the fallout.

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:33.880
Hey, maybe the smoke monster will have better
luck?

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:34.930
Big screen bombs

00:01:34.930 --> 00:01:39.141
He may have proven that he can handle himself
on a film set with his smaller outings, but

00:01:39.141 --> 00:01:42.850
his should-be blockbuster debut Speed Racer
was a car wreck.

00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:47.870
It had a bloated budget and a lot of expectations
behind it, but critics hated it, and it lost

00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:49.550
a ton of money at the box office.

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:53.600
His big screen career had no hatch hideaway
to shelter from this box office bomb.

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:57.480
The good news for Fox is that he was never
really held accountable for the film's poor

00:01:57.480 --> 00:01:58.480
performance.

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:00.600
But the wheels were already rolling in the
wrong direction.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:02.260
Then, Alex Cross happened.

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:06.670
Past adaptations of James Patterson's Alex
Cross novels have done fairly well — movies

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:09.060
like Kiss the Girls and Along Came a Spider.

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:14.260
But Alex Cross failed to live up to its predecessors,
despite some serious effort on Fox's part.

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:19.180
In the film, Fox played super bad guy Picasso,
who tortured and maimed people for sport.

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:23.600
The actor reportedly dropped a whopping 20
percent of his weight to play the villain,

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:26.780
and shed his former image as the heroic Jack
from Lost.

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:31.819
But despite how convincingly he played Picasso,
the movie was absolutely trashed by critics

00:02:31.819 --> 00:02:34.420
and — even worse — ignored by audiences.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:35.420
Ouch.

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:36.450
Cutting room floor

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:40.450
Fox got one more shot in a film that actually
did really well at the box office.

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:44.270
Too bad that his role was chopped to the point
that no one knew he was actually in it.

00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:48.740
The adaptation of Max Brooks' zombie epic
World War Z was supposed to be something else

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:50.840
than what audiences saw in theaters.

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:55.690
But after the original cut was shot, a large
chunk of the script was rewritten and reshot.

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:58.910
That left most of Fox's scenes on the editing
room floor.

00:02:58.910 --> 00:03:03.130
Fox would've starred as a colleague of Brad
Pitt's Gerry Lane, caring for Lane's family

00:03:03.130 --> 00:03:07.489
while he's off globe-trotting in an effort
to stifle the undead epidemic, but his role

00:03:07.489 --> 00:03:10.170
became a blink-and-you'd-miss-it parajumper
scene.

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:12.920
"That’s our target, get us down."

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:14.080
Seriously, that was it.

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:15.650
Hope you didn’t blink...

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:16.930
All the wrong headlines

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:22.350
In August 2011, Fox's name was dragged through
the mud as he was accused by a Cleveland woman

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:25.870
of punching her in the "arms, right leg, thighs
and chest."

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:31.750
Later, his former Lost co-star Dominic Monaghan
claimed on Twitter in 2012 that "he beats

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:33.599
women" as a reference to that event.

00:03:33.599 --> 00:03:38.550
The woman's suit was ultimately dropped and
Fox strongly denied the claims, but his reputation

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:39.800
was already sullied.

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:43.440
Fox denied the allegations completely in an
interview with Ellen — but it's hard to

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:45.879
undo damage like that once it's been done.

00:03:45.879 --> 00:03:50.161
Fox may have maintained his innocence of the
assault charges he faced, but in 2012, he

00:03:50.161 --> 00:03:52.569
was guilty of an entirely different crime.

00:03:52.569 --> 00:03:56.510
He was arrested for driving under the influence
in his home state of Oregon.

00:03:56.510 --> 00:04:00.661
He did fess up to that incident on Ellen,
insisting that he learned a hard lesson and

00:04:00.661 --> 00:04:02.010
that he'd never do that again.

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:07.160
Even so, the combination of these tabloid-frenzied
incidents certainly didn't help to elevate

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:08.709
his public profile.

00:04:08.709 --> 00:04:09.800
Break from Hollywood

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:14.240
Even before things started to slow down for
Fox's professional life, he'd already been

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:17.169
considering stepping away from the spotlight
for a while.

00:04:17.169 --> 00:04:21.049
Instead of living in Los Angeles like so many
other stars, he lives in Oregon, where he

00:04:21.049 --> 00:04:23.319
likes to fly planes and hang out with his
family.

00:04:23.319 --> 00:04:28.240
He told Men's Fitness in 2012 that he was
considering retiring from the industry even

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:32.570
then, saying that if he didn't "get quality
opportunities" he'd probably step away from

00:04:32.570 --> 00:04:33.570
the scene.

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:36.030
Seems like he had a contingency plan in place
the whole time!

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:40.710
But, for Fox fans hoping to see more of the
actor, the good news is that he hasn't altogether

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:42.839
disappeared from the entertainment industry.

00:04:42.839 --> 00:04:48.080
In 2015, he appeared in a pair of little-seen
horror pics, Extinction and Bone Tomahawk,

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:51.919
the latter of which was very well received
by critics, if not by audiences.

00:04:51.919 --> 00:04:55.590
So, it seems he's not completely done with
movies and television just yet.

00:04:55.590 --> 00:04:59.560
In the meantime, we can watch endless Lost
reruns and try to make heads or tails of what

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:01.900
was actually happening on that dumb island.

00:05:05.449 --> 00:05:07.759
It's the mystery that keeps on giving.

00:05:07.759 --> 00:05:08.759
Thanks for watching!

00:05:08.759 --> 00:05:11.469
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:11.469 --> 00:05:13.729
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love too!

